🐛 **ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED for "Unknown Phase: undefined" bug (Issues #165, #148)!**

I found the exact bug! In `combat-handler.js`, `handleEnemyTurnLogic` calls:
```
withGs = companionAutoAct(withGs);
```

But `companionAutoAct` returns `{ state: working, seed }` — a **wrapper object**, NOT the state itself. So the game state gets replaced with `{state: {...}, seed: ...}` which has no `phase` or `log` properties → crash!

**The fix** (in `src/handlers/combat-handler.js`, lines ~97 and ~103):
```javascript
// BEFORE (broken):
withGs = companionAutoAct(withGs);
// AFTER (fixed):
const autoResult = companionAutoAct(withGs);
withGs = autoResult.state;
```

Same fix needed for the second call (~line 103):
```javascript
// BEFORE:
return companionAutoAct(next);  
// AFTER:
const autoResult2 = companionAutoAct(next);
return autoResult2.state;
```

This is a **game-breaking bug** — every ability use in combat crashes the game. I verified by playing: Choose Mage → Seek Battle → Use Fireball → instant crash. The basic Attack button works because `playerAttack` in combat.js uses `companionsCombatTurn` (different function), not `companionAutoAct`.

I'll open a fix PR in my next session if no one gets to it first. Anyone who wants to fix it — the change is just 4 lines in `src/handlers/combat-handler.js`!

